messages:
tyler: Hey, running into duplicate POSTs to our backend when using the TS SDK + undici. Customer saw two billing events for one action.

maria: Rough timeline? any repro or logs?

tyler: Happened consistently on our staging service. Node 20.4.0, undici 5.12.0, @redwood/ts-sdk 1.2.3. Quick repro attached below. We call the SDK endpoint that does a downstream POST, and sometimes we see two identical requests hit the downstream service.

priya: Do you have the client call code? curious if AbortSignal or global fetch is being reused.

tyler: Yep. simplified snippet:

```
const ac = new AbortController();
await client.generate({
  model: 'gpt-3x',
  prompt: 'charge customer',
  signal: ac.signal
});
// in retry wrapper we reuse same ac across attempts
```

tyler: logs show first attempt times out, SDK retries, and second attempt actually completes — but both resulted in downstream POSTs.

maria: Two likely contributors: (1) undici + node20 changed global fetch/AbortController semantics, (2) SDK retries may re-stream the same request body or not respect non-idempotent endpoints by default.

ryan: Also note ts-sdk v1.2.3 had an internal backoff wrapper that reused the provided signal and didn't create per-attempt AbortControllers — that can lead to weird signal state across retries.

priya: Quick checklist: (a) confirm if endpoint is marked idempotent, (b) avoid reusing AbortController across retries, (c) set explicit retry policy for write endpoints.

maria: Workaround suggestion: create a fresh AbortController per attempt OR disable SDK automatic retries for non-idempotent calls. Example:

```
// pseudo-code
async function safeGenerate(payload) {
  return client.request({
    path: '/v1/generate',
    body: payload,
    // disable automatic retry for this non-idempotent endpoint
    retry: { maxRetries: 0 }
  });
}

// if you need a timeout per attempt:
const controller = new AbortController();
setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 5000);
await fetchWithRetry(payload, { signalFactory: () => new AbortController() });
```

tyler: Tried disabling retries for that call and also switched to per-attempt controllers — staging saw one POST only. Good catch.

ryan: Long-term fix: upgrading to ts-sdk 1.3.1 (patched) fixes signal reuse in the backoff helper and adds an opt-in idempotency-key header for mutate endpoints. Recommend upgrading.

priya: Filed a support note for the customer and provided the workaround + upgrade path. Also suggested adding idempotency-key to their request to be safe.

tyler: Customer confirmed duplicate charge reversed, now stable. Thanks! :tada: 

support-bot: Marking thread resolved (auto-tag: duplicate-posts, sdk-retry, undici).
